---
import HomeLayout from '../../layouts/HomeLayout.astro';
import { modernReviews } from '../../data/review-registry';
import '../../styles/review.css';
import '../../styles/beans.css';
import '../../styles/bean-guides.css';

const date='2026-10-20';
const path='/grinder/best-grinders-for-switching-regular-and-decaf/';
const canonical='https://coffeedant.com'+path;
const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/?$/,'/');
const local=(p:string)=>base+p.replace(/^\//,'');
const title='Best Espresso Grinders for Switching Between Regular and Decaf';
const description='A research-led US guide to four exact grinders and routines for switching regular and decaf beans, with retention limits, dial return, cleaning, tradeoffs and full reviews.';
const specs=[
  {slug:'/grinder/eureka-mignon-zero-65-all-purpose/',best:'Electric espresso plus filter switching',evidence:'65 mm AP burrs, revolution-counting stepless dial and bellows; independent absolute retention remains nonzero',tradeoff:'The bellows and dial cost more and do not certify a clear next decaf dose',skip:'You need strict zero carryover or a lower-cost grinder',setting:'Count full dial turns plus final mark; weigh output and purge when changing beans'},
  {slug:'/grinder/fellow-opus-2/',best:'Lower-spend electric single dosing',evidence:'One stepless side dial, two cups and low retention in two independent sample protocols',tradeoff:'Owner retention reports differ; filter-first taste evidence is mixed',skip:'You expect a zero-purge decaf change or need a dedicated filter grinder',setting:'Record each bag and dial position; brush permitted grounds path'},
  {slug:'/grinder/1zpresso-k-ultra/',best:'Manual second-grinder separation',evidence:'Portable hand grinder with external stepped setting and measured single doses',tradeoff:'Every espresso dose takes physical effort; hand grinding can be slow',skip:'You make many daily drinks or cannot comfortably hand-grind',setting:'Use it only for one bean type if separation is the priority; still clean it'},
  {slug:'/grinder/timemore-sculptor/',best:'Electric single-dose control at a higher tier',evidence:'Published single-dose design and adjustment approach in the full review',tradeoff:'Higher spend and more setup than a simple manual separation plan',skip:'You only need an occasional decaf cup and already have a capable grinder',setting:'Mark both coffee settings and verify the first output after a change'}
];
const picks=specs.map(p=>({...p,review:modernReviews.find(r=>r.slug===p.slug)!}));
if(picks.some(p=>!p.review)) throw new Error('Regular/decaf guide references an unregistered grinder');
const sections=[
  {id:'selection',title:'The decision: how often do you switch?',paragraphs:[
    'A person who makes a regular espresso every morning and one decaf at night faces a different problem from a household alternating bags shot by shot. We selected four exact grinders with full Coffeedant reviews because they represent distinct ways to handle that change: a bellows-equipped electric single-doser, a lower-spend electric single-doser, a hand grinder used as a dedicated second path, and a higher-tier electric single-doser. We considered documented adjustment, dose handling, cleaning access, US availability and independent or owner evidence where available. This is a workflow shortlist, not a taste ranking. [1] [2] [3] [4]',
    'First decide what “switch” means for you. If a small amount of regular coffee in a later decaf dose is unacceptable, a dedicated grinder and separate handling tools are the most defensible practical separation. If a routine purge is acceptable, a single-dose grinder with reachable grounds path and repeatable marks may be convenient. No source here certifies a caffeine-free output from a grinder recently used for regular coffee. [5] [6]'
  ]},
  {id:'retention',title:'Retention is more than one number',paragraphs:[
    'Three quantities are often blurred: the difference between beans put in and grounds out for one dose, coffee that remains physically inside the grinder, and old coffee exchanged into the next dose. These are not interchangeable. Eureka reports about 0.55 g total retention for the Zero 65 AP under its own method; Kaffeemacher found 1.8 g absolute retention in its independent protocol. The disagreement is a measurement boundary, not a basis for choosing the smallest number. [5] [6]',
    'Bon Appétit and The Coffee Chronicler each reported low output differences on their Opus 2 samples, but owners posted different outcomes. A bellows, ionizer or magnetic cup can reduce mess and carryover without proving that every internal surface is clean. If you alternate regular and decaf, weigh a few ordinary doses, purge according to the exact manual and watch what comes out after a setting change. Do not assign an invented percentage of caffeine transfer from a gram of retained grounds. [2] [7]'
  ]},
  {id:'settings',title:'Return to a setting without copying a stranger’s number',paragraphs:[
    'The Zero 65 AP dial has a revolution counter, so a large move from espresso toward filter can be written as a full turn count plus final mark. Opus 2 has a single 0–10 stepless side dial. K-Ultra uses an external stepped adjustment. Sculptor has its own adjustment mechanism. Each can supply a reference, but burr state, bag, roast date, humidity and basket can change the correct espresso grind. A saved number is a starting point, not an extraction guarantee. [1] [2] [3] [4]',
    'Keep two cards: regular bean and decaf bean. Note dose, beverage yield, basket, grinder position and date on each card. When switching, follow the grinder’s safe cleaning and purge instructions, then confirm the first shot or brew. If decaf is only occasional, maintaining a separate hand grinder can be simpler than repeatedly moving an electric dial. If every user wants electric espresso, the effort tradeoff reverses.'
  ]},
  {id:'cost',title:'Pay for the routine you will use',paragraphs:[
    'The selected US Zero 65 AP 110 V listing was $499 on October 20, 2026. The standard black Opus 2 was $199.95 in its October 15 review, with a backorder noted at that check. These are dated base prices for exact variants, not current checkout promises. Timemore and K-Ultra prices depend on exact version and seller; use their linked reviews and current cart rather than a stale cross-market table. [1] [2]',
    'A single expensive “zero retention” grinder may not solve a strict separation need. A dedicated second hand grinder, second electric grinder or careful shared-grinder purge each has a different cash, counter-space and labor cost. Add a scale, separate bean containers and cleaning time. If you only drink decaf occasionally, choose the least complicated method you will actually maintain.'
  ]},
  {id:'care',title:'Clean for the exact model',paragraphs:[
    'Unplug before accessing burrs. Follow each manufacturer’s permitted cleaning path; a video for a different Mignon, first-generation Opus or different Timemore variant can have different screws and clearances. Dry-brush where allowed, keep water out of electrical parts, and reassemble before another dose. A bellows is for loose coffee, not a substitute for periodic care. [8] [9]',
    'The first regular-to-decaf change on a new grinder is a good time to measure your own routine rather than trusting a marketing name. Record input and output masses, note visible retained grounds, clean as directed and compare the next dose. That does not measure residual caffeine, but it can expose a workflow that regularly leaves much more coffee behind than you expected.'
  ]}
];
const faqs=[
  {q:'Can one grinder switch between regular and decaf?',a:'Yes, with measured single doses, a repeatable setting record and a cleaning or purge routine. The evidence here does not certify zero regular-coffee carryover.'},
  {q:'Does a “zero retention” grinder leave literally no coffee inside?',a:'No. Eureka and independent Kaffeemacher figures for the Zero 65 AP are both nonzero and use different protocols.'},
  {q:'Which choice gives the clearest practical separation?',a:'A dedicated grinder assigned to one bean type avoids a routine cross-bean switch. It still requires normal cleaning and careful separate bean handling.'},
  {q:'Should I purge before the first decaf dose?',a:'Follow the exact grinder manual and your own tolerance. A purge can reduce old grounds but no quantified caffeine clearance was verified here.'},
  {q:'Is a hand grinder suitable for espresso?',a:'The reviewed K-Ultra supports espresso adjustment, but hand effort per dose is a real cost. Check basket and recipe on the actual bag.'},
  {q:'Can I use one grinder setting for both coffees?',a:'Rarely assume so. Save separate positions and dial each bag against a fixed dose and beverage target.'},
  {q:'Are the listed US prices current at checkout?',a:'No. They are dated product-review checks; verify exact voltage, finish, availability, tax and shipping with the seller.'}
];
const sources=[
  ['Eureka Zero 65 AP official product','https://www.eureka.co.it/en/products/eureka%2B1920/prosumer%2Bgrinders/zero%2Brange/118/','Exact model, burr, dial, bellows and factory claims.'],
  ['Fellow Opus 2 official product','https://fellowproducts.com/collections/grinder/products/opus-2-conical-burr-grinder','Second-generation dial, cups, US variant and single-dose design.'],
  ['1Zpresso K-Ultra official product','https://1zpresso.coffee/product/kultra/','Manual grinder identity and external adjustment; see full review for exact evidence.'],
  ['Timemore Sculptor 078S official product','https://www.timemore.com/products/timemore-electric-coffee-grinder-sculptor-series','Select the exact 078S variant, distinct from 078 and 064S.'],
  ['Kaffeemacher Zero comparison','https://kiffeemacher.com/en/blogs/kaffeewissen/eureka-zero-vergleichstest','Independent sample protocol and meaning of temporary, permanent and absolute retention.'],
  ['Kaffeemacher Eureka grinder compendium','https://kaffeemacher.ch/en/blogs/kaffeewissen/eureka-mills','Zero 65 AP absolute retention and other sample measurements.'],
  ['The Coffee Chronicler Opus 2 review','https://coffeechronicler.com/fellow-opus-2-review/','Independent sample filter, espresso and retention context; not a universal tolerance.'],
  ['Clive Zero 65 AP manual','https://support.clivecoffee.com/en/articles/16426660-eureka-mignon-zero-65-ap-espresso-grinder-user-manual','Exact-model startup and care boundary.'],
  ['Fellow Opus 2 safety manual','https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0057/6235/1219/files/Fellow_Opus2_SafetyManual_789-00291_F.pdf?v=1777654475','Exact-generation cleaning and electrical precautions.'],
  ['Bon Appétit grinder testing','https://www.bonappetit.com/story/best-coffee-grinder','Separate Opus 2 low-retention sample protocol.']
];
const cite=(p:string)=>p.replace(/\[(\d+)\]/g,(_m,n)=>'<a class="bean-cite" href="#s'+n+'" aria-label="Source '+n+'">['+n+']</a>');
const author={'@type':'Person',name:'Aleksandar Spasevski',jobTitle:'Editor, Coffeedant',url:'https://coffeedant.com/about/',image:'https://coffeedant.com/images/author-aleksandar-spasevski.jpg'};
const schema={'@context':'https://schema.org','@graph':[
  {'@type':'Article','@id':canonical+'#article',headline:title,description,genre:'Research-led grinder buying guide',inLanguage:'en-US',datePublished:date,dateModified:date,author,mainEntityOfPage:canonical,image:picks.map(p=>p.review.image),citation:sources.map(s=>s[1]),publisher:{'@type':'Organization',name:'Coffeedant',url:'https://coffeedant.com/'}},
  {'@type':'ItemList','@id':canonical+'#shortlist',name:title,itemListElement:picks.map((p,i)=>({'@type':'ListItem',position:i+1,name:p.review.brand+' '+p.review.model,url:'https://coffeedant.com'+p.slug}))},
  {'@type':'BreadcrumbList',itemListElement:[{'@type':'ListItem',position:1,name:'Home',item:'https://coffeedant.com/'},{'@type':'ListItem',position:2,name:'Grinders',item:'https://coffeedant.com/grinder/'},{'@type':'ListItem',position:3,name:title,item:canonical}]},
  {'@type':'FAQPage',mainEntity:faqs.map(f=>({'@type':'Question',name:f.q,acceptedAnswer:{'@type':'Answer',text:f.a}}))}
]};
---
<HomeLayout title={title+' | Coffeedant'} description={description} canonicalPath={path} image={picks[0].review.image} imageAlt={picks[0].review.imageAlt} ogType="article" published={date} updated={date}>
  <main id="main-content" class="review-page bean-buying-guide" data-guide-kind="grinders">
    <div class="review-shell">
      <nav class="review-breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href={base}>Home</a><span>/</span><a href={local('/grinder/')}>Grinders</a><span>/</span><span>Regular and decaf</span></nav>
      <header class="bean-guide-header"><p class="review-overline">Grinder buying guide · research-led · United States</p><h1>{title}</h1><p class="bean-lead">Choose the routine you can repeat. A single-dose design can reduce old grounds, but the name “zero retention” cannot certify a clean next decaf dose.</p><aside class="review-author-card"><div class="review-author-head"><img src={local('/images/author-aleksandar-spasevski.jpg')} alt="Aleksandar Spasevski, editor at Coffeedant" width="46" height="46" /><div><strong>Aleksandar Spasevski</strong><small>Editor, Coffeedant</small></div></div><p>Published and checked <time datetime={date}>October 20, 2026</time> · US product context</p><p>I compared exact grinder documentation, independent sample results and bounded owner context. Coffeedant has not ground, measured or tasted with these units. The picks are workflow judgments.</p></aside></header>
      <nav class="bean-jump" aria-label="Guide sections"><strong>Choose your routine</strong>{sections.map(s=><a href={'#'+s.id}>{s.title}</a>)}<a href="#quick-compare">Comparison</a><a href="#picks">The picks</a><a href="#faq">FAQ</a><a href="#sources">Sources</a></nav>
      <article class="bean-article">
        {sections.slice(0,2).map(s=><section class="review-section" id={s.id}><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">Decision and evidence</p><h2>{s.title}</h2></header><div class="review-section-body">{s.paragraphs.map(p=><p set:html={cite(p)} />)}</div></section>)}
        <section class="review-section" id="quick-compare"><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">Four different routines</p><h2>Quick comparison</h2></header><div class="bean-guide-table" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Scrollable regular and decaf grinder comparison"><table><caption>Exact reviewed products; no measured zero-carryover claim</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Grinder</th><th scope="col">Best role</th><th scope="col">Repeatability aid</th><th scope="col">Main limit</th></tr></thead><tbody>{picks.map(p=><tr><th scope="row"><a href={local(p.slug)}>{p.review.brand} {p.review.model}</a></th><td>{p.best}</td><td>{p.setting}</td><td>{p.tradeoff}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></section>
        <section class="review-section" id="picks"><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">Exact grinders, specific jobs</p><h2>Four defensible picks</h2></header><div class="bean-index-grid">{picks.map(p=><article class="bean-guide-pick"><img src={p.review.image} alt={p.review.imageAlt} width="360" height="360" loading="lazy" decoding="async" /><div><p class="review-overline">{p.best}</p><h3><a href={local(p.slug)}>{p.review.brand} {p.review.model}</a></h3><p><strong>Evidence:</strong> {p.evidence}.</p><p><strong>Tradeoff:</strong> {p.tradeoff}.</p><p><strong>Skip if:</strong> {p.skip}.</p><p class="bean-credit"><a href={p.review.links[0]?.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Image and product: {p.review.brand}</a>. Manufacturer or seller media for identification; no Coffeedant test photo.</p><a class="bean-guide-review-link" href={local(p.slug)}>Read the full review →</a></div></article>)}</div></section>
        {sections.slice(2).map(s=><section class="review-section" id={s.id}><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">Make the switch repeatable</p><h2>{s.title}</h2></header><div class="review-section-body">{s.paragraphs.map(p=><p set:html={cite(p)} />)}</div></section>)}
        <section class="review-section" id="related"><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">Related decisions</p><h2>Complete the station</h2></header><div class="bean-alternatives"><a href={local('/grinder/')}><strong>All grinder reviews</strong><span>Compare the electric and manual routes.</span></a><a href={local('/coffee-beans/best-decaf-coffee-beans-by-brew-method/')}><strong>Decaf beans by brew method</strong><span>Choose a bag for the drink you actually make.</span></a><a href={local('/coffee-beans/counter-culture-even-keel-half-caff/')}><strong>Half-caff alternative</strong><span>One premixed bag can simplify a different caffeine routine.</span></a></div></section>
        <section class="review-section" id="methodology"><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">Evidence and limits</p><h2>How this guide was made</h2></header><div class="review-section-body"><p>We selected exact currently reviewed products by adjustment return, single-dose handling, accessible cleaning, US configuration and the practical cost of a second grinder. Manufacturer retention claims, independent samples and owner anecdotes keep their own measurement contexts. Coffeedant has not ground, tasted, measured carryover or tested these units side by side.</p><p>Prices are dated where stated and are not current offers. This guide does not certify caffeine-free output after regular beans and does not convert retained-ground mass into a caffeine amount. A dedicated grinder is the straightforward separation choice when any carryover is unacceptable. Affiliate links do not determine selection.</p></div></section>
        <section class="review-section" id="faq"><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">Quick answers</p><h2>Regular and decaf grinder FAQ</h2></header><div class="bean-faq">{faqs.map(f=><article><h3>{f.q}</h3><p>{f.a}</p></article>)}</div></section>
        <section class="review-section" id="sources"><header class="review-section-heading"><p class="review-overline">Trace the claims</p><h2>Sources</h2></header><ol class="review-source-list">{sources.map((s,i)=><li id={'s'+(i+1)}><a href={s[1]} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{s[0]} ↗</a><p>{s[2]} Checked October 20, 2026.</p></li>)}</ol></section>
        <section class="final-verdict"><p class="review-overline">The practical choice</p><h2>Choose a repeatable separation routine</h2><p>Use one grinder with a documented purge and setting record when small carryover is tolerable. Assign a separate grinder to decaf when it is not. Confirm the routine on the exact unit and beans you own.</p><a class="review-buy-button review-buy-button-dark" href={local('/grinder/')}>Explore all grinders →</a></section>
      </article>
    </div>
  </main>
  <script is:inline type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema).replace(/</g,'\\u003c')} />
</HomeLayout>
